# Add-product

Reference: `src/app/(app)/cutting-orders/OrderDetailsPanel.tsx` (the **Add a product** box).

When the user says **add-product**, reuse this instead of a lone Combo, an Add row on the Fit List, or a modal picker. The button list itself is **products-button-list-picker**.

## Chrome

- **Centered** single box: stone-100 header bar (**Add a product**), then a segmented **button-list**.
- Equal-width buttons (`grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr`). Filled (stone-900) while that button’s popup is open.
- At most **15** buttons: **Any** first, then the first **14** items with `in_set = true` (name order). Extra in-set items are still reachable via **Any**.

## Picker

- Press a button → small popup **under that button**. If the button is near the **right edge**, shift the popup left so the full window stays in the panel. Combo Box of **active** merchandise whose lot is the **selected order lot** and whose `brand_id` matches the cutting order. Item buttons also filter `models.item_id`. **Any** skips the item filter (still that lot only).
- Combo label is `products.name` when set, else lot>model title.
- **New** (small red, like add-lot) opens a create-product popup for the **selected order lot**. Lot is locked. Model Combo is the item button’s item, or any model if **Any**. Same merchandise fields as New product (collection, price, stage, availability, size/drop). Header **Upcharges** (after a model) opens a sibling popup with the `$ extra` matrix, stretched left to the panel edge; Escape closes that popup first. Create does not attach until **Add**.
- **Add** inserts the line (`status` true / Open) and closes; duplicate → “Already on this order.”
- **Cancel** or Escape closes the popup only (does not close a docked panel).

Do not put an **Add** row on the Fit List that this picker feeds.
